    "THE RELATIONSHIP TYPES the wizard's matrix offers, as ONE table read by the client (client/src/constants/relationships.ts) and the server (server/lib/relationships.js).",
    "",
    "The wizard stores the LOCALIZED label of the chosen type per ordered character pair, so the server can only recognise a relationship by matching that label against this table. Each type has a stable typed key (what code branches on), its labels and the key of its inverse. The two sentinels (not set / strangers) live in shared/relationship-sentinels.json and are not types.",
    "",
    "Customers fill the matrix in either direction ('Ludovica Genitore di Mamma' means Ludovica is the parent OF Mamma, the wrong way round), so code that asks 'is A the parent or child of B' must accept both parentOf and childOf. A label that is not in this table (custom or legacy) maps to null; it is never guessed.",
    "",
    "Swiss German: ss, never the eszett."
